---
import StandardPageLayout from "../../layouts/StandardPageLayout.astro";
import Glossary from "../../components/Glossary.astro";
import PageToc from "../../components/PageToc.astro";
import "../../styles/standards-poster.css";
import "../../styles/extended.css";
import HistoryTimeline from "../../components/HistoryTimeline.astro";
import history from "../../data/history.json";
import metadata from "../../data/standards/aspe/aspe3800.json";
---

<StandardPageLayout
  code={metadata.code}
  standardType={metadata.framework}
  title={metadata.title}
  description={metadata.description}
  issued={metadata.issued}
  latestAmendment={metadata.latestAmendment}
  status={metadata.status}
  summary={metadata.summary}
  bannerNotice={metadata.bannerNotice}
>
  <Fragment slot="toc">
    <PageToc
      items={[
        { id: "s1", label: "Conceptual Framework Linkage" },
        { id: "s2", label: "Scope" },
        { id: "s3", label: "Recognition Criteria — Reasonable Assurance" },
        { id: "s4", label: "THE PRESENTATION CHOICE — Asset-Related Government Assistance" },
        { id: "s5", label: "Income-Related Government Assistance" },
        { id: "s6", label: "Forgivable Loans" },
        { id: "s7", label: "Repayment of Previously Recognized Assistance" },
        { id: "s8", label: "Worked Example — Deducting Assistance From an Asset's Cost" },
        { id: "s9", label: "Worked Example — Deferred Income Presentation for the Same Grant" },
        { id: "s10", label: "Disclosure Requirements" },
        { id: "s11", label: "Critical Judgments &amp; Estimates" },
        { id: "s12", label: "Relationship to IAS 20 and Contrast With ASC 832" },
        { id: "s13", label: "Statement Mapping" },
        { id: "s14", label: "Related Standards" },
        { id: "s15", label: "Glossary" }
      ]}
    />
  </Fragment>
  <div class="wrap">
</div>





<div class="section-header" id="s1"><span class="num">1</span><h2>Conceptual Framework Linkage</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Full recognition and measurement, not merely disclosure</div><div class="principle">ASPE Section 3800 governs the RECOGNITION, MEASUREMENT, and PRESENTATION of GOVERNMENT assistance — TRANSFERS of resources TO an ENTERPRISE by A government, IN return FOR past OR future COMPLIANCE with SPECIFIED conditions. THE Section OFFERS genuine PRESENTATION choices, BROADLY converged WITH IAS 20 internationally (Section 4).</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s2"><span class="num">2</span><h2>Scope</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Grants, forgivable loans, and other government transfers</div><div class="principle">This Section applies TO government GRANTS, forgivable LOANS, and OTHER forms OF government ASSISTANCE — EXCLUDING investment TAX credits, WHICH are GOVERNED separately BY Section 3805 (see the COMPANION poster), GIVEN their SPECIFIC interaction WITH the income TAX system.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s3"><span class="num">3</span><h2>Recognition Criteria — Reasonable Assurance</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Compliance and receipt must both be reasonably assured</div><div class="text-supporting">GOVERNMENT assistance IS recognized WHEN there IS reasonable ASSURANCE that the ENTERPRISE will COMPLY with the CONDITIONS attached TO the assistance, AND that the ASSISTANCE will ACTUALLY be RECEIVED — BOTH conditions MUST be MET together.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s4"><span class="num">4</span><h2>THE PRESENTATION CHOICE — Asset-Related Government Assistance</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">Deduct from asset cost, or defer and amortize</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1fr 2fr;"><span>Approach</span><span>Description</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1fr 2fr;"><span>Cost reduction approach</span><span>THE assistance IS deducted FROM the COST of the RELATED depreciable ASSET, REDUCING future DEPRECIATION expense OVER the ASSET'S useful LIFE</span></div>
<div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1fr 2fr;"><span>Deferred income approach</span><span>THE assistance IS recorded AS deferred INCOME, RECOGNIZED in NET income OVER the SAME periods AS the RELATED costs it IS intended TO compensate</span></div>
</div>
<div class="text-supporting">AN enterprise ELECTS ONE of these TWO approaches AS an ACCOUNTING policy — BOTH produce the SAME net INCOME over TIME, but DIFFER in PRESENTATION (a SMALLER asset AND lower DEPRECIATION, VERSUS a FULL-cost asset PAIRED with SEPARATELY amortized DEFERRED income).</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s5"><span class="num">5</span><h2>Income-Related Government Assistance</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Presented as income, or as a reduction of the related expense</div><div class="text-supporting">GOVERNMENT assistance NOT tied TO a SPECIFIC depreciable ASSET (e.g. a WAGE subsidy, OR an OPERATING cost REIMBURSEMENT) is RECOGNIZED in NET income — EITHER presented AS a SEPARATE item OF income, OR as a REDUCTION of the RELATED expense it IS intended TO offset.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s6"><span class="num">6</span><h2>Forgivable Loans</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Recognized as assistance once forgiveness conditions are reasonably assured</div><div class="text-supporting">A FORGIVABLE loan (a LOAN the GOVERNMENT agrees TO waive REPAYMENT of, PROVIDED specified CONDITIONS are MET) is recognized AS government ASSISTANCE when THERE is reasonable ASSURANCE that the ENTERPRISE will MEET the TERMS for FORGIVENESS — UNTIL that POINT, it is ACCOUNTED for SIMPLY as a LIABILITY (an ORDINARY loan).</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s7"><span class="num">7</span><h2>Repayment of Previously Recognized Assistance</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Adjusting the asset or recognizing an immediate expense</div><div class="text-supporting">WHERE previously RECOGNIZED government ASSISTANCE becomes REPAYABLE (e.g. a CONDITION is SUBSEQUENTLY breached), the REPAYMENT is ACCOUNTED for AS a CHANGE in ESTIMATE — INCREASING the CARRYING amount OF the related ASSET (WHERE the cost-REDUCTION approach was USED) or RECOGNIZING an IMMEDIATE expense (WHERE the DEFERRED income APPROACH was used AND no DEFERRED balance REMAINS).</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s8"><span class="num">8</span><h2>Worked Example — Deducting Assistance From an Asset's Cost</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">A smaller asset base, lower future depreciation</div>
<div class="worked" style="margin-bottom:0;"><div class="wk-title">Example: A capital grant for new equipment</div><div class="wk-body">A company purchases equipment for $1,000,000, receiving a $200,000 government grant toward the purchase, with reasonable assurance of compliance and receipt. The equipment has a 10-year useful life. The company elects the cost reduction approach.</div><div class="wk-answer">The COMPANY records the EQUIPMENT at $1,000,000 − $200,000 = $800,000, DEPRECIATING it AT $800,000 ÷ 10 = <strong>$80,000 per year</strong> — RATHER than THE $100,000 per YEAR it WOULD otherwise HAVE recognized.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s9"><span class="num">9</span><h2>Worked Example — Deferred Income Presentation for the Same Grant</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Full-cost asset, paired with separately recognized deferred income</div>
<div class="worked" style="margin-bottom:0;"><div class="wk-title">Example: The same facts, electing the deferred income approach</div><div class="wk-body">Continuing the prior example, the company instead elects the deferred income approach.</div><div class="wk-answer">The COMPANY records the EQUIPMENT at ITS FULL $1,000,000 cost, DEPRECIATING it AT $100,000 per YEAR, WHILE SEPARATELY recognizing $200,000 ÷ 10 = <strong>$20,000 per year</strong> of DEFERRED grant INCOME — the NET effect on ANNUAL income ($100,000 depreciation − $20,000 grant INCOME = $80,000 net EXPENSE) is IDENTICAL to the COST-reduction approach.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s10"><span class="num">10</span><h2>Disclosure Requirements</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">What Section 3800 requires</div><div class="check-list"><span>Nature and extent of government assistance recognized during the period</span><span>Accounting policy adopted (cost reduction or deferred income approach) for asset-related assistance</span><span>Unfulfilled conditions and other contingencies attaching to recognized assistance</span></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s11"><span class="num">11</span><h2>Critical Judgments &amp; Estimates</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cn span2"><div class="ctitle cn">Where judgment matters most</div>
<div class="two-col"><div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT JUDGMENTS</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Whether reasonable assurance of compliance and receipt genuinely exists</span><span>Which presentation approach (cost reduction or deferred income) to elect</span></div></div>
<div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT ESTIMATES</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Periods over which deferred income should be recognized, matched to the related costs</span></div></div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s12"><span class="num">12</span><h2>Relationship to IAS 20 and Contrast With ASC 832</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Comparison — ASPE Section 3800 vs IAS 20 vs US GAAP ASC 832</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1.1fr 1fr 1fr;"><span>Feature</span><span style="color:var(--color-text-warning);">ASPE Section 3800</span><span style="color:var(--color-text-info);">IAS 20</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.1fr 1fr 1fr;"><span>Recognition/measurement guidance</span><span>Full, prescriptive</span><span>Full, prescriptive — converged</span></div>
<div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1.1fr 1fr 1fr;"><span>Presentation choices</span><span>Asset cost reduction OR deferred income</span><span>Same choice — converged</span></div>
</div>
<div class="note">GENUINELY thoroughly CONVERGED with IAS 20 — the SHARP contrast LIES with US GAAP'S OWN ASC 832 (COVERED earlier in THIS library'S US GAAP SERIES), WHICH deliberately PROVIDES no RECOGNITION or MEASUREMENT guidance AT all, LEAVING diversity IN practice INTACT. ASPE, LIKE IAS 20, TAKES the OPPOSITE, fully PRESCRIPTIVE approach.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s13"><span class="num">13</span><h2>Statement Mapping</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">Where every government assistance event lands</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Event</span><span>Statement(s) affected</span><span>Notes</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Asset-related assistance</span><span><span class="badge bs">BS</span> <span class="badge is">IS</span></span><span>Reduces asset cost, or deferred and amortized separately</span></div>
<div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Income-related assistance</span><span><span class="badge is">IS</span></span><span>Recognized as income or expense reduction</span></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s14"><span class="num">14</span><h2>Related Standards</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Cross-reference map</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>Section</span><span>Connection</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>Section 3805</span><span>Investment Tax Credits — a related, but separately governed, form of government support specific to the tax system</span></div>
<div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>Section 3061</span><span>Property, Plant and Equipment — supplies the depreciation mechanics affected by the cost reduction presentation choice</span></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s15"><span class="num">15</span><h2>Quick-Reference Glossary</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cn span2">
<div class="glossary-item"><div class="glossary-term">Cost reduction approach</div><div class="glossary-def">Deducting government assistance from the cost of the related depreciable asset, reducing future depreciation expense.</div></div>
<div class="glossary-item" style="border-bottom:none;"><div class="glossary-term">Forgivable loan</div><div class="glossary-def">A loan whose repayment the government agrees to waive if the enterprise meets specified conditions, recognized as assistance once forgiveness is reasonably assured.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="legend"><div class="ltitle">Financial statement key (ASPE terminology)</div><div class="lrow"><div class="litem"><span class="badge bs">BS</span> Balance Sheet </div><div class="litem"><span class="badge is">IS</span> Income Statement </div><div class="litem"><span class="badge sre">SRE</span> Statement of Retained Earnings / Statement of Changes in Equity </div><div class="litem"><span class="badge scf">SCF</span> Cash Flow Statement</div></div></div>


</div>
  </div>
  <section id="history">
    <HistoryTimeline items={history.aspe3800 || []} />
  </section>
</StandardPageLayout>
